      "explanation": "**Correct Answer: A**\n\nIn an unfolded cube net, faces separated by one square become **opposite faces** on the folded cube.\nOpposite faces can **never** be adjacent or visible at the same time:\n\u2022 **Circle (\u25cb)** and **Plus (+)** are opposite.\n\u2022 **Cross (\u2715)** and **Diamond (\u25c7)** are opposite.\n\u2022 **Solid Dot (\u25cf)** and **Triangle (\u25b3)** are opposite.\n\nThe other options erroneously depict opposite faces simultaneously on the same cube. Only the correct option displays three mutually adjacent faces with zero opposing pairs.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 **Speed Tip:** Immediately identify opposite face pairs on the net; any option showing both opposite faces simultaneously is impossible.",
